diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b7822d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Feature: Clear completed
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can quickly clean up my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden when there are no completed todos
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is visible when there are completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is visible
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..be0112b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Feature: Todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos I have
+  So that I can gauge my remaining work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows zero items when there are no todos
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows the number of active todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter uses singular form for one item
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter uses plural form for multiple items
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
diff --git a/features/creating-todos.feature b/features/creating-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c91f21b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/creating-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+Feature: Creating todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: A new todo is created when the user presses Enter with non-empty text
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the first todo is not completed
+    And the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: A new todo is not created when the user presses Enter with empty text
+    When the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: A new todo is not created when the user presses Enter with whitespace only
+    When the user types "   " in the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: The new todo input is trimmed before creating
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos can be created sequentially
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the second todo has title "Walk the dog"
diff --git a/features/deleting-todos.feature b/features/deleting-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fe351af
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/deleting-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Feature: Deleting todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove todos I no longer need
+  So that my task list stays relevant
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes a todo
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user clicks the destroy button of the first todo
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo does not affect other todos
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user clicks the destroy button of the first todo
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f0c812
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct mistakes or update task details
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo
+    Then the first todo element has class "editing"
+    And the edit input of the first todo has value "Buy groceries"
+    And the edit input of the first todo is focused
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit and exits editing mode
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input of the first todo
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the first todo element does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the edit
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input of the first todo
+    And the edit input of the first todo loses focus
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy organic groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input of the first todo
+    And the user presses Escape
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the first todo element does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an empty edit deletes the todo
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo
+    And the user clears the edit input of the first todo
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Saving a whitespace-only edit deletes the todo
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo
+    And the user types "   " in the edit input of the first todo
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
diff --git a/features/filtering.feature b/features/filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e6592c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Filtering todos
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by their status
+  So that I can focus on specific subsets of my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: All todos are shown by default
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the "All" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: The Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
+    And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: The Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user clicks the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the "Completed" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: The filter is applied when navigating via hash
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: A todo updated while filtered is hidden if it no longer matches
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter
+    And the user navigates to "#/"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox of the first todo
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
diff --git a/features/mark-all-complete.feature b/features/mark-all-complete.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..313e037
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/mark-all-complete.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Mark all as complete
+  As a user
+  I want to toggle all todos at once
+  So that I can efficiently manage my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox marks all todos as completed
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox marks all todos as active
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a completed todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are not completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox reflects the state of all todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox of the second todo
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4191494
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my data
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the first todo is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo is completed
+
+  Scenario: The localStorage key is "todos-todomvc"
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    Then localStorage contains key "todos-todomvc"
diff --git a/features/toggling-todos.feature b/features/toggling-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dc75b09
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggling-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Feature: Toggling todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox of the first todo
+    Then the first todo is completed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox on a completed todo marks it as active
+    Given a completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox of the first todo
+    Then the first todo is not completed
+
+  Scenario: The completed class is toggled on the todo item
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox of the first todo
+    Then the first todo element has class "completed"
diff --git a/features/visibility.feature b/features/visibility.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ea2e146
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/visibility.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Feature: Section visibility
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show only relevant sections
+  So that the interface stays clean
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: The main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: The main section and footer are shown when there are todos
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+
+  Scenario: The main section and footer are hidden after all todos are deleted
+    Given a todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When the user clicks the destroy button of the first todo
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
